      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. its definitely a lot more professional now. \n\none thing though, i was lookin at the original transcript again and i noticed the way the customer was talking... it's pretty much all slang and not really following standard grammar rules, right? like \"nobody doin nothin\" and \"it still ain't show up.\" \n\nas a communications specialist, how would you characterize that type of speech in a formal report? like if we were explaining to the management team why this specific call was difficult to process or why we need to train staff on how to handle it, how would you describe the customer's level of professionalism or clarity?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
